# Mosquitto ACL for anonymous (unauthenticated) clients in PROD mode.
# Rider apps connect with no credentials and consume the public transit
# position stream. They can NEVER publish (no `write` rule below) and
# cannot read anything outside `transit/#`.
#
# Drivers and the backend authenticate via the go-auth plugin — this file
# is irrelevant to them; their permissions come from the API's
# /internal/mqtt-auth/acl endpoint.
#
# Mosquitto ACL syntax: topic-rules that appear BEFORE any `user` line
# apply to anonymous clients. `pattern` uses %u/%c substitutions and
# requires authentication, so it doesn't fit here.

topic read transit/#
